<title>USA: Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are movie ticket sales at the U.S. box office for the June 20-22 weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Sunday. Final data will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p> 1 (*) Batman &amp; Robin .......................... $43.6 million</p>
<p> 2 (*) My Best Friend's Wedding ................ $21.5 million</p>
<p> 3 (2) Con Air ................................. $10.2 million</p>
<p> 4 (3) Jurassic Park: The Lost World ...........  $8.0 million</p>
<p> 5 (1) Speed 2: Cruise Control .................  $7.2 million</p>
<p> 6 (5) Austin Powers ...........................  $1.4 million</p>
<p> 7 (6) Gone Fishin' ............................  $1.2 million</p>
<p> 8=(4) Addicted To Love ........................  $900,000</p>
<p> 8=(8) The Fifth Element .......................  $900,000</p>
<p> 10(7) Buddy ...................................  $820,000</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parentheses. * denotes new release.</p>
<p>&quot;Batman &amp; Robin&quot; and &quot;Addicted To Love&quot; are released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;My Best Friend's Wedding&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. Sony's Columbia Pictures unit released &quot;Buddy&quot; and &quot;The Fifth Element.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Con Air&quot; and &quot;Gone Fishin'&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Speed 2: Cruise Control&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
</text>
